// `kama.json` manifest + `@compileFor` (Stage 2). The manifest (this dir's kama.json) DECLARES the
// user flags WINDOWS/LINUX/TELEMETRY and marks TELEMETRY `"default": true`. It is auto-discovered next
// to this source, which enables strict validation (an undeclared flag would be rejected — see the
// guard tools/check-compilefor.sh). This is a default (debug / native) build with no --define, so:
//   TELEMETRY -> on (default)   WINDOWS -> off (declared, not activated)
// giving 40 + 2 = 42. Both sides of each gate are defined, so every build resolves the call.
@compileFor(TELEMETRY)  fn int32 tel()  { return 40; }
@compileFor(!TELEMETRY) fn int32 tel()  { return 0; }

@compileFor(WINDOWS)    fn int32 plat() { return 99; }
@compileFor(!WINDOWS)   fn int32 plat() { return 2; }

fn int32 main() { return tel() + plat(); }
